e, etc., Josh 10:21 ( J E ; object of I. חָרַץ q. v., compare 3 below), Jer 18:18 ; Isa 3:8 ׳ זַעַם ל Hos 7:16 (but text dubious, compare We Now ), חֶרֶב חַדָּה ׳ ל Ps 57:6 , compare Ps 64:4 כְּמוֺ ׳ נָחָשׁ שָֽׁנְנוּ ל Ps 140:4 תָּקוּם אִתָּךְ ׳ כָּללֿ Isa 54:17 ׳ הֶאֱרִיךְ ל Isa 57:4 further, Jer 9:2 ; Jer 9:4 as instrument of seductive flattery ( הֶחֱלִיק ), without בְּ , Ps 5:10 ; Prov 28:33 , compare ׳ נָכְרִיָּה חֶלְקַת לָ Prov 6:24 . of falsehood Ps 78:36 (compare below); of slander (compare לושֵׁן ) ׳ רָגַל עַללֿ Ps 15:3 , אִישׁ לָשׁוֺן Ps 140:12 , compare סָ֑תֶר ׳ לְ Prov 25:33 ׳ חָטָא בְּל Ps 39:2 compare Ps 64:9 (text dubious, see Hup Che Bae ); moral qualities ascribed to: — as arrogant Ps 12:5 (compare v Ps 12:4 above); as devising injuries, ׳ הַוּוֺת תַּחְשֹׁב ל Ps 52:4 , compare הַוֺת ׳ לְ Prov 17:4 תַּצְמִיד מִרְמָה ׳ ל Ps 50:19 nectere fraudem ; ׳ מֵרָ֑ע נְצֹר ל Ps 34:14 ׅ || (וּשְׂפָתֶיךָ מִדַּבֵּר מִרְמָה ; often of lying tongue: לְשׁוֺן שֶׁקֶר Prov 6:17 ; Prov 12:19 ; Prov 21:6 ; Prov 26:28 ; Ps 109:2 מִרְמָה ׳ לְ Ps 52:6 רְמִיָּה ׳ לָ Mic 6:12 ; Ps 120:2 ; Ps 120:3 תַּרְמִית ׳ לְ Zeph 3:13 תַּהְפֻּכוֺת ׳ לְ Prov 10:31 , and ׳ נֶהְפָּךְ בִּל Prov 17:20 עֲרוּמִים ׳ ל Job 15:5 also מִרְמָה דִּבֵּ֑ר ׳ ל Jer 9:7 on the other hand צַדִּיק ׳ לְ Prov 10:20 חֲכָמִים ׳ ל Prov 12:18 ; Prov 15:2 ׳ מַרְפֵּה לָ v Prov 15:4 לִמּוּדִים ׳ לְ Isa 50:4 . — Note phrases ׳ שׁוֺט ל Job 5:21 scourge of (the) tongue , רִיב לְשֹׁנוֺת Ps 31:21 פַּלַּג לְשׁוֺנָם Ps 55:10 : also ׳ בַּעַל הַלּ Eccl 10:11 (of serpent-charmer), and ׳ וַתֵּעֲלוּ עַלשְֿׂפַת ל Ezek 36:3 . — On tongue of ׳ י (once), see 4 below \\ \\ c. organ of singing, subject of רָנַן Ps 51:16 ; Ps 126:2 ; Isa 35:6 , עָנָה Ps 119:172 . 2. = language Deut 28:49 ; Jer 5:15 and later, namely: Ezek 3:5 ; Ezek 3:6 ( ׳ כִּבְדֵי ל , || עִמְקֵי שָׂפָה , but strike out ᵐ5 Manuscripts Co Sgfr KauAT ), Isa 28:11 (|| אַחֶרֶת ׳ ל , לַעֲגֵי שָׂפָה , figurative of ׳ י 's unintelligible dealings); ׳ עַם ֗֗֗ נִלְעַג ל Isa 33:19 (|| עִמְקֵי שָׂפָה ); Isa 66:18 (|| גּוֺיִם ), Zech 8:23 ; Gen 10:5 ; Gen 10:20 ; Gen 10:31 (all P ), Neh 13:24 ; Esth 1:22 (twice in verse); Esth 3:12 ; Esth 8:9 (twice in verse); Dan 1:4 . 3. tongue of animals: dog Exod 11:7 ( J ; object of I. חָרַץ q. v.; compare 1 b ), Ps 68:24 adder Job 20:16 (subjectof תַּהֲרֹג ); crocodile Job 40:25 . 4. tongue of fire, devouring, כֶּאֱכֹל קַשׁ לְשׁוֺן אֵשׁ Isa 5:24 compare of ׳ י , וּלְשׁוֺנוֺ כְּאֵשׁ אֹכָ֑לֶת Isa 30:27 (|| שְׂפָתָיו מָֽלְאוּ זַעַם ). 5. = ( tongue- shaped) wedge of gold Josh 7:21 ; Josh 7:24 ( J E ). ** So Assyrian lišânu ; see Meissn ZAW xxlii {1905}, 151 f. Johns Assyrian Deeds 2, 281 . 6. = ( tongue- shaped) bay of sea Isa 11:15 ; Josh 15:2 ; Josh 15:5 ; Josh 18:19 (all P ).", "definition_html": "<h1><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4473')\">BDB4473</entry> [<entry onclick=\"sn('H3956')\">H3956</entry>]</h1><div class=\"navigation\"><entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4472')\">BDB4472</entry> | BIBLICAL HEBREW | <entry onclick=\"bdbid('BDB4474')\">BDB4474</entry></div><p> <bdbheb>לָשׁוֺן</bdbheb> <b>noun masculine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Josh 7:21\" b=\"6\" cBegin=\"7\" vBegin=\"21\" cEnd=\"7\" vEnd=\"21\" onclick=\"bcv(6,7,21)\">Josh 7:21</ref></sup> and (more often) <b>feminine</b><sup><ref ref=\"Isa 28:11\" b=\"23\" cBegin=\"28\" vBegin=\"11\" cEnd=\"28\" vEnd=\"11\" onclick=\"bcv(23,28,11)\">Isa 28:11</ref></sup> <highlightword>tongue</highlightword> (Late Hebrew <highlight>id.</highlight>; also Assyrian <transliteration><highlight>lišânu</highlight></transliteration>; Arabic <placeholder2863/>; Ethiopic <placeholder2864/>; Aramaic <bdbarc>לִשָּׁן</bdbarc>, <bdbheb>לִישָּׁן</bdbheb>, <placeholder2865/> (all <highlight>li-</highlight>); Zinjirli <bdbheb>לשן</bdbheb> <lookup onclick=\"bdbabb('DHM')\">DHM<sup>Sendsch. 59</sup></lookup>); — absolute <bdbheb>׳</bdbheb><bdbheb>ל</bdbheb> <ref ref=\"Exod 4:10\" b=\"2\" cBegin=\"4\" vBegin=\"10\" cEnd=\"4\" vEnd=\"10\" onclick=\"bcv(2,4,10)\">Exod 4:10</ref> +; <bdbheb>הַלָּשֹ